{"content":[{"c":["TIRHAKAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Ethiopian king who marched north to fight against the Assyrian army, thus diverting Sennacherib’s siege of Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.9","r":"2Kgs.19.9","rawR":"2Kgs.19.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.9","value":"2Kgs.19.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.37.9","r":"Isa.37.9","rawR":"Isa.37.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.37.9","value":"Isa.37.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 37:9"},"). The report of Tirhakah’s intended invasion prompted the Rabshakeh’s second threat against Jerusalem, Hezekiah’s prayer for deliverance, and the subsequent divine destruction of the Assyrian army (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.8-37","r":"2Kgs.19.8-37","rawR":"2Kgs.19.8-37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.8-37","value":"2Kgs.19.8-37"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:8-37"},"). Tirhakah is almost certainly the Egyptian king Taharqa, who ruled from 689–664 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," during the 25th (Ethiopian) dynasty. Tirhakah probably served as commander of the army while he was crown prince, so that the reference to him as “king” refers to his then-future position."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Tirhakah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.9","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.9","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.9"},{"anchorText":"Is 37:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.37.9","rawQueryValue":"Isa.37.9","sourceRefExact":"Isa.37.9"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:8-37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.8-37","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.8-37","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.8-37"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"60f84d50d77d1dc70204b8c77e5291538208fe5e19ee0165ee73061e6d5c95eb","sourceItemName":"Tirhakah","sourceItemOrder":174,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Tirhakah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Tirhakah","title":"Tirhakah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}